37. Final formula
For a loan:

$maximumLoanDeduction =
    $grossSalary * 0.25;

$loanInstallment =
    min(
        $remainingLoan,
        $maximumLoanDeduction
    );

Then:

$totalDeductions =
    $pfDeduction
    + $messDeduction
    + $leaveDeduction
    + $normalPenaltyTotal
    + $loanInstallmentTotal
    + $otherDeduction;

And:

$netSalary = max(
    0,
    round(
        $grossSalary - $totalDeductions,
        0
    )
);

38. Very important issue with your current index()
There is one more thing to fix.

Your index() is currently a preview calculation, while generate() actually writes payroll.

If you call:

GET /payroll?month=8&year=2026

before generating payroll, there may not yet be a loan installment row.

Therefore I would make the index behave as a calculation preview:

If installment exists:
    show actual installment

If installment does not exist:
    calculate what installment WOULD be

But do not create the installment from GET/index.

GET should not modify the database.

So for the preview:

$loanSummary = $loanRecoveryService->previewEmployeeLoanDeduction(
    $employee->id,
    $grossSalary,
    $month,
    $year
);

while generate() calls:

calculateEmployeeLoanDeduction()

and actually creates the installment.

This separation is important.

39. I recommend two service methods
Instead of only:

calculateEmployeeLoanDeduction()

make:

previewEmployeeLoanDeduction()

and:

createEmployeeLoanDeduction()

